## Dependencies

Before installing, make sure you have the following packages:

*   **Kitty:** `emerge x11-terms/kitty` (or your distro's package manager).
*   **Font:** **Hack Nerd Font** (required for icons to render correctly).
*   **Pywal (Optional but recommended):** `pip install pywal` (or `emerge app-misc/pywal`) for dynamic colors.

## Installation

1. **Clone the repository:**
   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com/kizill-top-jr/kizill-kitty-konf.git
   cd kizill-kitty-konf
   ```
   Backup your old config (just in case):
   bash
   ```bash
   cp ~/.config/kitty/kitty.conf ~/.config/kitty/kitty.conf.bak
   ```
  Copy the new configuration:
  ```bash
  cp kitty.conf ~/.config/kitty/
  ```
Color Scheme (Pywal)

The config includes a line that pulls colors from your Pywal cache:
```ini
include ~/.cache/wal/colors-kitty.conf
```
If you use Pywal:

Just run wal -i /path/to/your/wallpaper.jpg and restart Kitty. The colors will apply automatically.
If you DON'T use Pywal:

If you don't have Pywal installed, Kitty will throw an error on startup. Open ~/.config/kitty/kitty.conf and either delete or comment out the include line. Then define your own foreground, background, and color0 through color15 manually.

